Observe the spiral similairties at  $M, B, C$  mapping \[CA \stackrel{M}{\hookrightarrow} BD; TM \stackrel{B}{\hookrightarrow} AC; SM \stackrel{C}{\hookrightarrow} DB. \] Then  $\triangle MCA \sim \triangle MBD, \triangle BTM \sim \triangle BAC,$  and  $\triangle CSM \sim \triangle CDB$ . Therefore 
\begin{align*}
\frac{MS}{MT} &= \frac{\frac{BD}{BC} \cdot MC}{\frac{CA}{CB} \cdot MB} 
&= \frac{BD \cdot MC}{CA \cdot MB} 
&= \frac{BD \cdot \frac{MB}{BD} \cdot CA}{CA \cdot MB} 
&= 1, 
\end{align*} so that  $MS = MT$ , as desired.  $\blacksquare$

